In article <25113@cs.yale.edu> beigel-richard@CS.YALE.EDU (Richard Beigel) writes:
...
>SEGV and BUS signals are usually errors, whereas HUP is not.  That is
>why nethack saves in the latter case.  When you restore after a SEGV
>or BUS error, does it usually work?  I suggest including a warning, like
>"Restoring saved game ...--More--
> Game saved after bus error.  Proceed at your own risk."

i've yet to have a problem running a game that was saved this way.  the
action generally starts up a move or two before the crash, and i make
a point of not doing the same thing again (for example, one time i
kicked a non-disappearing item immediately upon restart on the theory
that the crash had to do with a corpse i'd kicked which had just
disappeared).

the sample size here is probably 2-4 dumps.  i notice them alot less
now that i don't lose my game.

